    {
      "short": "TLS",
      "chapter": "solution",
      "title": "TLS at the front door",
      "body": [
        "<span class=\"term\">TLS</span> fixes all three. The load balancer presents a certificate for <code>mendly.health</code>, signed by an authority the browser trusts, proving it's the real site. The handshake agrees on fresh session keys, and everything after is encrypted and tamper-evident.",
        "The snooper now sees random bytes going to Mendly's address. But TLS ends at the load balancer — behind it, traffic still flows in plain HTTP across the internal network."
      ],
      "changes": [
        "+ HTTPS with a trusted certificate",
        "+ HTTP redirects to HTTPS",
        "~ Internal hops still plain"
      ],
