    {
      "short": "TLS inside",
      "chapter": "technique",
      "title": "No trusted inside",
      "body": [
        "Internal networks get breached too, and cloud networks are shared. So Mendly encrypts every hop: <span class=\"term\">mutual TLS</span> between load balancer and API — both sides present certificates — and TLS to the database.",
        "A service mesh or platform can issue and renew these short-lived internal certificates automatically, so no one forgets the one that expires on a Sunday. Modern CPUs make the encryption cost negligible."
      ],
      "changes": [
        "+ mTLS between internal services",
        "+ TLS to the database",
        "+ Automatic certificate renewal"
      ],
