    {
      "short": "At rest",
      "chapter": "solution",
      "title": "Encrypt what's on disk",
      "body": [
        "<span class=\"term\">Encryption at rest</span> protects stored data: the database volume and its backups are encrypted with AES-256. A lost backup drive or a disk pulled from a rack is just noise.",
        "Know its limit. The running database decrypts transparently for anyone it lets in — so a SQL injection or a stolen app credential still reads plaintext. Disk encryption guards hardware, not access."
      ],
      "callout": {
        "kind": "warn",
        "text": "\"Encrypted at rest\" on a checklist often means only disk encryption. Ask who can make the system decrypt."
      },
      "changes": [
        "+ Encrypted volumes and backups"
      ],
