    {
      "short": "Secrets mgr",
      "chapter": "solution",
      "title": "A safe for secrets",
      "body": [
        "Mendly moves every credential into a <span class=\"term\">secrets manager</span>. The API proves its identity — via its platform workload identity, not another password — and fetches the database credentials at startup.",
        "Secrets are encrypted (by the KMS), access is granted per service, and every read is audited. The code and config now hold only the <i>name</i> of a secret. A leaked repo leaks nothing usable."
      ],
      "changes": [
        "+ Secrets manager",
        "- Passwords in code and config",
        "~ API fetches credentials at startup"
