    {
      "short": "Rotation",
      "chapter": "insight",
      "title": "Assume keys leak; rotate them",
      "body": [
        "Any secret may leak eventually, so limit how long it's useful. <span class=\"term\">Rotation</span> replaces credentials on a schedule — and instantly after any suspected leak. Better still, the secrets manager issues <b>dynamic</b> database users that expire after an hour.",
        "Keys rotate too: the KMS creates a new master key version and new data keys get wrapped with it, while old versions stay available for decryption. Practise rotation regularly so it's a routine, not an emergency."
      ],
      "changes": [
        "+ Short-lived database credentials",
        "+ Yearly master-key rotation"
