      "chapter": "recap",
      "title": "Locked boxes: recap",
      "body": [
        "<ul class=\"takeaways\"><li><b>TLS everywhere</b> → secrecy, integrity and identity on every hop, inside too</li><li><b>At rest</b> → disk encryption guards hardware, not access</li><li><b>Envelope encryption</b> → data keys wrapped by a master key that never leaves the KMS</li><li><b>Secrets manager</b> → no credentials in code; access by identity, audited</li><li><b>Rotation</b> → short-lived secrets and rotated keys limit any leak</li></ul>"
